# SHEYTAN-LA line-ending policy (v1.10.8, W-A — run 38823624040 class)
#
# ROOT CAUSE this file fixes: windows-latest runners default to
# core.autocrlf=true; with no attributes file the checkout materialized
# every .go file as CRLF, and gofmt (which normalizes to LF) then listed
# the whole tree at the Windows gofmt gate — even though the committed
# tree is byte-for-byte gofmt-clean (Linux's identical gate is green on
# the same commit 22049b9). The gate was RIGHT; the checkout was wrong.
# This policy fixes the ENVIRONMENT, never the gate.
#
# SCOPE — deliberately minimal (no blanket `* text eol=lf`):
#
#   *.go  -> text eol=lf
#     Every tracked .go file is stored LF in the index (verified:
#     `git ls-files --eol -- '*.go'` reports i/lf for all 548 files), so
#     this pin causes zero renormalization; it only guarantees the
#     working tree gofmt observes is the same LF tree on every platform,
#     Windows included. The gofmt gate itself is untouched.
#
#   *.bat -> text eol=crlf
#     JUSTIFIED ADDITIONAL LINE (the only one): the Windows launcher
#     packaging/SHEYTAN-LA.bat uses goto-label control flow, which
#     cmd.exe parses reliably only with CRLF. Its historical Windows
#     materialization was CRLF (via the runners' autocrlf=true default);
#     the v1.10.8 Windows checkout pin (core.autocrlf=false) would
#     otherwise silently change that to LF. This line PRESERVES the
#     launcher's native endings; the index copy stays LF exactly as
#     committed, so nothing is renormalized.
#
#   LICENSE.md + internal/brand/brand_license_body.md -> text eol=lf
#     The sole license artifact and its go:embed twin must stay LF so
#     brand.LicenseText and root LICENSE.md compare equal after the
#     releasecontract EOL normalizer on every platform (Windows run
#     40685008386: CRLF embed made TestLicenseSyncContractSurvivesWindowsLineEndings
#     fail by turning existing \r\n into \r\r\n).
#
# Everything else (installer sources under packaging/nsis, docs, web
# assets, baselines) keeps repository-native endings: NSIS accepts both
# endings and no other tool in the pipeline normalizes line endings.
*.go text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
LICENSE.md text eol=lf
internal/brand/brand_license_body.md text eol=lf
